1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:03,880
Before taking over a command
workstation, check which application

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,349
and environment you are using.

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:09,560
We begin in IC's Calls workspace,
with the department's training

4
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,000
incidents already listed.

5
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:14,439
Open the menu at the upper
left and choose Settings.

6
00:00:14,899 --> 00:00:20,360
At the top, App Info shows App Name,
Version and Environment; this example

7
00:00:20,389 --> 00:00:23,000
identifies Resgrid IC in development.

8
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:26,620
That gives a command aide useful
details when reporting a problem.

9
00:00:27,069 --> 00:00:31,600
For practice, locate those three
values, then find the Account section

10
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:35,409
directly underneath before reviewing
connection or sign-in settings.

11
00:00:35,549 --> 00:00:40,059
In Settings, Account, open Server
to inspect the connection address.

12
00:00:40,489 --> 00:00:44,650
The form shows Custom and a
complete Server URL; the loopback

13
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:47,610
address here belongs to this
local training environment.

14
00:00:47,999 --> 00:00:51,440
Use the address supplied by your
administrator for your own installation.

15
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,860
The note says to leave off the API
version path and a trailing slash.

16
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,440
Cancel closes this review without
saving a different server.

17
00:00:59,819 --> 00:01:03,560
During a command handover, comparing
the address first helps avoid

18
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,520
troubleshooting the wrong installation.

19
00:01:05,909 --> 00:01:08,700
Practice finding the complete
address rather than relying

20
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,179
on the shortened Account row.

21
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,320
Back in Account, choose
Sign-in and security.

22
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:16,399
Read each section as the
current account's summary.

23
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:21,040
Here, Authenticator app says it
is not set up, and Passkeys for

24
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:22,799
this app says there are none yet.

25
00:01:23,210 --> 00:01:27,000
Responder approvals lists
Macintosh with Approvals stopped.

26
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:31,649
Recent verifications reports no
verifications in the last thirty days.

27
00:01:32,059 --> 00:01:36,090
These are separate facts, so check
each rather than treating one heading

28
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:37,760
as a general security verdict.

29
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:41,029
If your department requires
another method, arrange its

30
00:01:41,029 --> 00:01:42,479
approved setup separately.

31
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:46,619
This review does not enroll an
authenticator or create a passkey.

32
00:01:46,859 --> 00:01:50,850
In Account, Login Info opens
the Username and Password form.

33
00:01:51,339 --> 00:01:54,600
Both fields are empty in this
demonstration, and Cancel and

34
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,169
Save are visible together.

35
00:01:56,610 --> 00:02:01,589
Save submits these details to sign in; it
is not an account password-change screen.

36
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:06,420
For a routine workstation review, leave
the fields empty and choose Cancel.

37
00:02:06,799 --> 00:02:10,420
This is especially useful when a
supervisor is showing a colleague where

38
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:14,990
account access lives: you can explain the
form without putting anyone's credentials

39
00:02:14,990 --> 00:02:17,199
into a shared presentation or recording.

40
00:02:17,419 --> 00:02:21,129
In Account, Shared device is the
place to review a workstation

41
00:02:21,129 --> 00:02:22,740
used by several operators.

42
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:27,250
The page explains the shared-session
purpose, shows This is a shared

43
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:31,210
device switched on, and offers a
Device label, which is optional.

44
00:02:31,599 --> 00:02:34,739
The important note says this
takes effect the next time

45
00:02:34,739 --> 00:02:36,519
someone signs in on this device.

46
00:02:36,939 --> 00:02:40,839
The form shown here has not been
saved, so its switch alone does not

47
00:02:40,839 --> 00:02:42,730
prove a shared policy is active.

48
00:02:43,089 --> 00:02:46,909
Before a shift handover, compare
this choice with department guidance

49
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:48,530
and decide who should configure it.

50
00:02:48,749 --> 00:02:53,219
Lower in Settings, Preferences groups
the display and device choices.

51
00:02:53,770 --> 00:02:57,749
Theme currently shows System,
while Language shows Select option.

52
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:02,409
Keep Alive is off, and BT
Handset says No device selected.

53
00:03:02,909 --> 00:03:06,269
Check these displayed states before
assuming a workstation has your

54
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:09,859
preferred presentation or audio
arrangement; this browser view

55
00:03:09,859 --> 00:03:13,709
does not demonstrate a connected
handset or a device staying awake.

56
00:03:14,219 --> 00:03:19,660
Immediately below, Support lists Help
Center, Contact Us, System Status,

57
00:03:19,830 --> 00:03:22,109
Privacy Policy and Terms of Service.

58
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:26,839
For practice, identify the appropriate
support destination without opening

59
00:03:26,839 --> 00:03:28,639
an external page during this review.

60
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:33,530
In Settings, Sync and Offline Queue
shows a Sync Status of Up to date.

61
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:36,599
Choose View Sync Queue
for the detailed picture.

62
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:41,619
This session is Online, with zero
pending, zero failed and zero done,

63
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:44,060
and the center says Queue is empty.

64
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:48,509
The queue actions are disabled because
there is nothing here to process or clear.

65
00:03:48,929 --> 00:03:52,959
An empty queue is a useful handover
check, but it does not demonstrate an

66
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:55,039
offline write or successful replay.

67
00:03:55,439 --> 00:03:58,650
Practice reading connectivity
and all three counts together

68
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:01,739
before describing the current
sync state to another operator.

69
00:04:01,899 --> 00:04:06,289
Finally, in Account, choose
Logout to read Confirm Logout.

70
00:04:06,769 --> 00:04:11,279
The warning says logout will clear
app data, cached values and settings.

71
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:15,819
Choose Cancel to finish this review
while keeping the session; an actual

72
00:04:15,819 --> 00:04:17,430
logout is a separate decision.

73
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:22,169
The same checks help a fire or EMS
command aide, a community crisis

74
00:04:22,169 --> 00:04:27,430
coordinator, a search-and-rescue lead, a
security supervisor, a wildland command

75
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:29,969
team or an industrial response desk.

76
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:34,170
In each setting, a useful handover
names the environment, account

77
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:38,200
state and current queue rather than
leaving the next operator to guess.

